# The provider-only bundle (OFXPLUGIN_CUDA_FROM_HOST=ON) in Resolve Studio 21.2.0.5, 2026-11-26.
#
# Two packages, same switch:
#   1.32.0 GPU package -> the host refuses the plug-in
#   1.20.1 GPU package -> the host loads it, applies it, renders one frame
#
# Why the difference is a packaging fact, not a bug in the switch: the provider DLL
# is what the host has to load, and it imports a specific CUDA major.

## 1. what the bundles contain (no cuDNN, cuBLAS, cuFFT or cudart of ours)

bundle (1.32.0 package): OnnxInference.ofx, onnxruntime-ofx.dll, onnxruntime_providers_cuda.dll, onnxruntime_providers_shared.dll
bundle (1.20.1 package): the same four files
build log, 1.32.0: -- CUDA provider bundle: provider only (OFXPLUGIN_CUDA_FROM_HOST=ON). The host must supply cuDNN 9, cuBLAS/cuBLASLt 12, cuFFT 11 and the CUDA 12 runtime; the bundle ships none of them, so it cannot create a second copy of a base name the host has loaded.

## 2. what the provider DLL imports (dumpbin /dependents)

## 1.32.0 package
    cublasLt64_13.dll
    cublas64_13.dll
## 1.20.1 package
    cublasLt64_12.dll
    cublas64_12.dll
    cufft64_11.dll
    cudart64_12.dll
    cudnn64_9.dll

