## What this says

# The switch does what it is for: the bundle ships no cuDNN, cuBLAS, cuFFT or cudart,
# and the host's process keeps its own cudnn64_9.dll from its install folder. No second
# module of a base name enters the process.
#
# It does not by itself make the bundle loadable: the provider imports cuBLAS 13 in the
# 1.32.0 package and cuBLAS 12 in the 1.20.1 one, and Resolve 21.2 ships 12. Build the
# provider-only bundle against a runtime whose CUDA major matches the host.
#
# The frame is a pass-through: Resolve's scripted OFX effect exposes GetInfo, GetIndex,
# GetIsEnabled, SetIndex and SetIsEnabled and nothing else, so the model parameter cannot
# be set and render() never runs. A device render in Resolve needs a project that already
# carries the parameter value - not a script.
